WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.779
After 20th Century Fox's final attempt to
revive the Fantastic Four for a feature film

00:00:05.779 --> 00:00:11.250
failed miserably, news of Marvel Studios'
plans to do their own Fantastic Four movie

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.450
was warmly received, to say the least.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.090
And now there are rumours flying about that
the team's big-screen comeback could introduce

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.860
a seriously powerful comic book character.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:25.410
We Got This Covered is reporting that Disney
and Marvel are considering introducing the

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:30.160
mighty mutant Franklin Richards to the Marvel
Cinematic Universe through their forthcoming

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.009
Fantastic Four reboot.

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:35.930
Now, it's important to take this with a grain
of salt, We Got This Covered didn't provide

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.560
really anything to substantiate this rumor,
and the website has proved less than reliable

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.560
in the past.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:47.310
But hey, who can resist a little Fantastic
speculation every now and then?

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:51.120
"Flame on!"

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.450
Described by the site as "the most powerful
superhero to ever appear in Marvel Comics,"

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:02.640
Franklin Richards is the child of the Fantastic
Four's iconic couple: Sue Storm and Reed Richards.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.810
The Richards famously developed their superhuman
powers after being exposed to cosmic radiation

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:13.000
during a space flight expedition, but their
son obtained his powers at birth.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.030
Created by comics legends Jack Kirby and Stan
Lee and first appearing in 1968's Fantastic

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:24.380
Four Annual Issue 6, Franklin was born after
a pregnancy that nearly killed his mother.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:29.200
His genetic structure is altered like his
parents', meaning Franklin's superhuman powers

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.840
manifested fast and furiously.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.780
In the vein of his fellow Omega-level mutants,
Franklin's full power registers beyond any

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.780
definable limit.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.900
In fact, his capabilities are so impressive
that he's even been compared to Marvel's Celestials,

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:48.600
a race of humanoid aliens who came into being
around the same time as the universe itself.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:54.020
In the future, Franklin will actually be one
of only two beings around to witness the total

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.060
end of the universe.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.720
Franklin has been a part of so much throughout
the Fantastic Four's long history in the Marvel

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.830
universe, so it's difficult to get a concrete
grasp on how he would fit into the Fantastic

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.040
Four reboot.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.989
Any number of Franklin's iterations could
feature in the forthcoming flick, from his

00:02:10.989 --> 00:02:15.580
early days in the Power Pack, a team of kids
who possess superhuman powers, to his role

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.319
in the Human Torch-less Future Foundation.

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:23.590
And a backstory that rich could easily present
a ton of headaches for Marvel Studios' creatives

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.410
as they try to figure out a way to introduce
Franklin to the MCU.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.989
Would all that effort even be worth it?

00:02:29.989 --> 00:02:34.099
It's hard to say for sure, but this is far
from the first time Franklin's been rumored

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:36.790
to appear in a Fantastic Four film.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:43.019
In June 2017, Fox reportedly considered bringing
Franklin Richards into the live-action sphere.

00:02:43.019 --> 00:02:47.669
According to Bleeding Cool, there were rumors
that Fox was eyeing a possible kid-centric

00:02:47.669 --> 00:02:53.059
film set in the Fantastic Four universe that
featured Franklin and his younger sister Valeria,

00:02:53.059 --> 00:02:56.359
along with appearances by The Thing and the
Human Torch.

00:02:56.359 --> 00:03:01.439
Those rumors resurfaced in July 2017, around
the time that it was announced that Legion

00:03:01.439 --> 00:03:05.430
showrunner Noah Hawley had a Doctor Doom film
in development.

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:10.230
And while Fox seemed more than happy to forget
about the entire 2015 Fantastic Four reboot

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:14.639
debacle, it did appear that the studio was
interested in mining the heroes' considerable

00:03:14.639 --> 00:03:16.549
cinematic universe potential.

00:03:16.549 --> 00:03:21.769
Now that Fox and Disney have merged, it's
likely that Disney has scrapped Fox's previous

00:03:21.769 --> 00:03:26.299
plans for any Fantastic Four-adjacent characters
in favor of their own.

00:03:26.299 --> 00:03:30.859
On the flip side, the studio convergence has
apparently paved the way to reboot heaven,

00:03:30.859 --> 00:03:35.799
with Disney CEO Bob Iger already confirming
that Fox properties such as Home Alone and

00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:39.840
Night at the Museum will take on a new life
at Disney+.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:45.049
Disney is clearly invested in expanding its
family-centric narratives, and though the

00:03:45.049 --> 00:03:50.219
Fantastic Four franchise will probably fall
into line with the rest of the MCU, Franklin's

00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:55.200
rumored arrival could open up the chance for
more of a family-focused superhero team-up.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.339
At the end of the day, though, this is all
just talk.

00:03:58.339 --> 00:04:03.150
Until Marvel comes forward with concrete information
about the new Fantastic Four movie, all fans

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:06.159
can do is speculate on what the future might
hold.

